#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""AGNI — routed multi-system agent harness.

One LLM tool loop over routed subsystems (HADES-style dispatch hierarchy:
deterministic CLIs > headless browser > device UI). Core routes:

    bitwarden  -> `bw`                 vault status/unlock + credential retrieval
    github     -> `gh`                 repos, PRs, issues, gh api
    gog        -> `gog`                Google Workspace (Gmail/Calendar/Drive)
    browser    -> `browser-use`        rendered web automation (sitemaps/profiles)
    android    -> `adb`                Android device/emulator control
    ios        -> `xcrun simctl`       iOS simulator control
    auth       -> login pipeline       bw unlock -> cred fetch -> browser fill
                                       (secrets stay in-process, never logged)

Usage:
    agni "check my github notifications, then reply to the unread calendar invite"
    agni auth <site> [--url <login_url>]   # deterministic login pipeline
    agni --doctor                          # subsystem binary + auth report
    agni --routes                          # print the routing table
    agni --dry-run "..."                   # print tool calls, don't execute

Env:
    AGNI_MODEL       model name                  (default: gpt-4o)
    AGNI_BASE_URL    OpenAI-compatible API base  (default: https://api.openai.com/v1)
    OPENAI_API_KEY   API key (or AGNI_API_KEY)
    AGNI_MAX_TURNS   max tool turns              (default: 30)
    BW_SESSION       existing Bitwarden session token (skips unlock)
    AGNI_BW_PASSWORD Bitwarden master password env for non-interactive unlock
    BU_CDP_URL       attach browser-use to an existing Chrome CDP endpoint
    BU_NAME          browser-use daemon session name (tab-per-job isolation)
"""

